It is derived from two inputs:

- Glosses: Wiktionary (https://en.wiktionary.org, CC BY-SA), via the
  kaikki.org machine-readable extract produced by wiktextract
  (https://kaikki.org/dictionary/Spanish/).
- Frequency ranking: doozan/spanish_data
  (https://github.com/doozan/spanish_data), which derives its counts from
  hermitdave/FrequencyWords (https://github.com/hermitdave/FrequencyWords),
  itself derived from OpenSubtitles2018
  (http://opus.nlpl.eu/OpenSubtitles2018.php).

Changes made: filtered to the top frequency-ranked content-word lemmas
(nouns, verbs, adjectives, adverbs), joined each to a single short English
gloss (skipping archaic, rare, and form-of senses), and reformatted as JSON.

All source code in this repository is MIT-licensed (see LICENSE). The license
split is intentional: CC BY-SA applies to the data file only, not to the code.
